@startuml
title T12-WF07 — AI Customer Segmentation Agent (Sequence)
autonumber
participant "Schedule Trigger" as SCHED
participant "n8n WF07\nSegmentation" as N8N
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
participant "Rule Engine\ninside NestJS" as RULE
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Gemini API" as AI

SCHED -> N8N: Segment refresh schedule
activate N8N
N8N -> API: GET active segment definitions
API -> DB: Read Segment records/rules
DB --> API: Active segments
API --> N8N: Segment definitions
loop For each segment
N8N -> API: GET eligible customer cohort/features
API -> DB: Read customer data/features
DB --> API: Cohort
API --> N8N: Customer cohort
N8N -> N8N: Validate/shape Rule Engine request only
N8N -> API: POST evaluate segment
API -> RULE: Evaluate using backend-owned rules
RULE -> DB: Read needed features and update assignments transactionally
DB --> RULE: Evaluation/assignment results
RULE --> API: Counts and assignment summary
API --> N8N: Segment evaluation result
N8N -> N8N: Normalize stats for reporting (no membership rules here)
end
N8N -> AI: Generate evidence-based segment insights from backend results
AI --> N8N: Summary/trend insights
N8N -> N8N: Validate that insights stay within returned evidence
N8N -> API: Save workflow execution summary
API -> DB: Persist WorkflowRun/output summary
DB --> API: Saved run ID
API --> N8N: Saved summary
opt Anomaly threshold exceeded
N8N -> API: Request in-app notification/task
API -> DB: Persist notification/audit
DB --> API: Notification record
API --> N8N: Accepted
end
deactivate N8N
note over N8N,RULE
n8n orchestrates the Rule Engine; it must not reimplement segment criteria
or directly assign CustomerSegment memberships.
end note
@enduml
